# .bf-paths — manifest of Blackfuel-additive paths.
#
# Source of truth for the change-classification rule defined in ADR-0003.
# Every file that lands on `main` is exactly one of:
#
#   * BF-additive — its path matches an entry below; never conflicts with
#     upstream sync because upstream will never create these paths.
#   * Upstream — anything else. Edits to upstream paths are [bf-patch]
#     commits and need an Upstream-status: trailer (enforced by
#     bf-patches-trailer-lint, planned).
#
# Syntax (.gitignore-style positive list):
#   * comments start with #
#   * blank lines ignored
#   * `path/` matches that directory and everything under it
#   * `path/**` is equivalent
#   * `bf-*.yml` matches anywhere shell-glob would
#   * `path/bf-*.yml` matches in a specific directory
#
# bf-lint.yml syntax-checks this file; bf-classification-lint.yml uses it
# to classify every PR's diff.

# Blackfuel-owned documentation tree (ADRs, agent context, runbooks).
bf-docs/

# Blackfuel-owned helper modules and scripts (version helper, release-
# notes generator, agent-log, etc. — added incrementally as the mirror
# grows).
bf-tools/

# Blackfuel-owned CI workflows. The bf- filename prefix is mandatory
# per ADR-0003; the sync workflow deletes any non-bf-*.yml workflow file
# on every merge so unprefixed inherited workflows never survive.
.github/workflows/bf-*.yml
.github/workflows/bf-*.yaml

# Blackfuel-owned composite actions shared by the bf-build-* workflows.
# Upstream ships no .github/actions/; the bf- dir prefix keeps them BF-owned.
# Glob (not a `/**` prefix) so the .bf-paths matcher's fnmatch branch honors
# the bf-* dir wildcard; fnmatch '*' spans '/', covering nested helper files.
.github/actions/bf-*/*

# Blackfuel-additive root Makefile. Upstream ships no Makefile at root,
# so this never conflicts. Extend with dev shortcuts (lint, fmt, etc.)
# as bf-vllm matures.
Makefile

# Self-reference: this manifest is Blackfuel-owned.
.bf-paths

# Blackfuel-owned PR/issue templates. Upstream ships its own
# PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md (we replaced it in PR #4 — that one stays a
# [bf-patch] for now because the path is upstream-owned). Anything we
# add under .github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/bf-*.md or similar is BF-additive.
.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/bf-*.md
.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/bf-*.yml

# Blackfuel-owned skill definitions (planned, per ADR-0006).
.claude/skills/bf-vllm-*/

# Blackfuel-owned actionlint config. Upstream ships no actionlint.yaml; we add
# one to declare the Blacksmith runner labels the bf-build-* workflows target
# (ADR-0005) so the actionlint pre-commit hook accepts them.
.github/actionlint.yaml

# Blackfuel-owned lightweight CPU benchmark image. Upstream ships no
# Dockerfile.cpu-bench or requirements/cpu-bench.txt — these are the build
# recipe for the `vllm-cpu-bench` tool image (a stripped-down CPU image for
# `vllm bench`), so the paths never conflict with an upstream sync even though
# they live in otherwise upstream-owned directories.
docker/Dockerfile.cpu-bench
requirements/cpu-bench.txt
